  "id": "self-guide",
  "term": "self-guide",
  "definition": "In self-discrepancy theory, a self-guide is a standard or image of attributes used to evaluate oneself. An ideal self-guide is the qualities a person wants to have, while an ought self-guide is the qualities another person believes the individual should have.",
